251
00:14:38,504 --> 00:14:40,304
It is not developing.

252
00:14:40,664 --> 00:14:41,754
It is being eaten.

253
00:14:42,824 --> 00:14:44,284
The Pattern.

254
00:14:44,344 --> 00:14:46,144
These are not cautionary tales.

255
00:14:46,644 --> 00:14:47,724
They are data points.

256
00:14:48,504 --> 00:14:52,744
Organize every collapsed economy by its total extractive burden, the combined

257
00:14:52,744 --> 00:14:54,344
share of G.D.P.

258
00:14:54,364 --> 00:14:58,544
consumed by military spending, corruption, crime, misallocation, and capital

259
00:14:58,544 --> 00:15:00,864
flight, and three bands emerge.

260
00:15:01,824 --> 00:15:04,224
thirty-five to forty-five percent:

261
00:15:04,264 --> 00:15:06,204
the death spiral begins.

262
00:15:06,644 --> 00:15:10,864
The Soviet Union (forty to fifty percent total extraction including the

263
00:15:10,864 --> 00:15:16,324
shadow economy), Yugoslavia (thirty-five to forty-five percent before dissolution,

264
00:15:16,584 --> 00:15:19,924
with the federal government spending fifty to sixty percent of its budget

265
00:15:19,924 --> 00:15:24,744
on the military alone and Serbia secretly issuing one point four billion

266
00:15:24,744 --> 00:15:30,044
dollars in credits to regime allies), Argentina (thirty-five to forty percent),

267
00:15:30,244 --> 00:15:32,624
Zimbabwe (forty to fifty-five percent).

268
00:15:33,864 --> 00:15:38,004
At this level, productive people start running the numbers and concluding

269
00:15:38,004 --> 00:15:40,364
that the numbers do not favor staying productive.

270
00:15:40,984 --> 00:15:42,194
Brain drain accelerates.

271
00:15:43,084 --> 00:15:44,544
Capital flees.

272
00:15:44,804 --> 00:15:47,584
The economist Mancur Olson identified the mechanism:

273
00:15:48,404 --> 00:15:52,624
when extraction is fragmented among competing actors, no single extractor

274
00:15:52,624 --> 00:15:56,124
has incentive to limit their take, because the cost of their extraction

275
00:15:56,124 --> 00:16:00,074
is spread across the whole economy while the benefit is theirs alone.

276
00:16:01,024 --> 00:16:02,884
Olson called them "roving bandits."

277
00:16:03,504 --> 00:16:05,924
Your civilization is manufacturing them at scale.

278
00:16:06,604 --> 00:16:11,164
Your military-industrial complex, your cybercrime syndicates, your corrupt

279
00:16:11,164 --> 00:16:12,014
institutions,

280
00:16:12,704 --> 00:16:14,664
each extracts independently.

281
00:16:14,784 --> 00:16:17,054
None internalizes the cost to the whole system.

282
00:16:17,764 --> 00:16:21,664
Total extraction exceeds the sustainable maximum not because any single

283
00:16:21,664 --> 00:16:25,824
actor is greedy, but because the structure makes restraint irrational.

284
00:16:27,544 --> 00:16:29,204
fifty to sixty-five percent:

285
00:16:29,824 --> 00:16:31,204
collapse becomes irreversible.

286
00:16:32,204 --> 00:16:36,944
Venezuela (sixty to seventy percent), Lebanon (fifty to sixty-five percent),

287
00:16:37,284 --> 00:16:41,684
Syria (forty-five to sixty-five percent, where one man's crony network controlled

288
00:16:41,704 --> 00:16:43,124
sixty percent of the economy),

289
00:16:43,784 --> 00:16:45,864
North Korea (fifty to sixty percent,

290
00:16:46,544 --> 00:16:48,904
spending twenty-two to twenty-four percent of G.D.P.

291
00:16:49,164 --> 00:16:52,344
on military alone before counting total state extraction).

292
00:16:53,404 --> 00:16:57,334
Recovery at this stage requires not reform but replacement.

293
00:16:57,764 --> 00:17:00,564
The institutions that could fix the problem ARE the problem.

294
00:17:01,204 --> 00:17:03,744
The people who could fix the institutions have left.

295
00:17:05,004 --> 00:17:06,164
seventy to ninety percent:

296
00:17:06,644 --> 00:17:07,774
failed state equilibrium.

297
00:17:08,944 --> 00:17:13,764
Somalia (eighty to ninety percent), Haiti (sixty to eighty percent),

298
00:17:14,404 --> 00:17:17,204
Democratic Republic of the Congo, or D.R.C.

299
00:17:17,244 --> 00:17:18,904
(fifty-five to seventy percent),

300
00:17:19,544 --> 00:17:23,784
Libya post-twenty fourteen (seventy to eighty percent, where oil accounts

301
00:17:23,784 --> 00:17:25,924
for sixty-five percent of G.D.P.

302
00:17:26,124 --> 00:17:29,744
and ninety-eight percent of government revenue, and militias decide who

303
00:17:29,744 --> 00:17:30,244
gets it).

304
00:17:30,984 --> 00:17:33,484
The productive economy is a rounding error.

305
00:17:34,344 --> 00:17:36,544
These countries are not "developing."

306
00:17:36,904 --> 00:17:37,874
They have reached equilibrium.

307
00:17:38,844 --> 00:17:40,484
The equilibrium is misery.

308
00:17:41,184 --> 00:17:41,924
And it is stable,

309
00:17:42,704 --> 00:17:45,504
because the extractive structure is self-reinforcing:

310
00:17:45,984 --> 00:17:49,884
the worse things get, the more rational extraction becomes, which makes

311
00:17:49,884 --> 00:17:50,704
things worse.

312
00:17:52,004 --> 00:17:55,104
The death spiral begins at thirty-five percent.

313
00:17:55,164 --> 00:17:56,004
Not fifty percent.

314
00:17:56,604 --> 00:18:00,444
The fifty percent number is where you end up after the spiral has been running

315
00:18:00,444 --> 00:18:03,204
for a while and everyone who could leave has left.

316
00:18:04,104 --> 00:18:05,944
By fifty percent, the patient is not sick.

317
00:18:06,724 --> 00:18:09,414
The patient is a skeleton that has not yet been informed.

318
00:18:10,484 --> 00:18:14,304
Professional observers call thirty-five percent terminal parasitic load:

319
00:18:14,924 --> 00:18:18,824
the point where enough of the economy is devoted to extraction that the

320
00:18:18,824 --> 00:18:23,484
death spiral becomes self-reinforcing and recovery without external intervention

321
00:18:23,484 --> 00:18:25,664
becomes historically unprecedented.

322
00:18:27,004 --> 00:18:30,624
Your global economy is running the same pattern at a larger scale.

323
00:18:31,184 --> 00:18:35,484
The difference is that when Venezuela crosses thirty-five percent, Venezuelans

324
00:18:35,484 --> 00:18:36,604
can flee to Colombia.

325
00:18:37,124 --> 00:18:41,204
When the global economy crosses thirty-five percent, there is no Colombia.

326
00:18:41,884 --> 00:18:45,204
The system does not need to reach fifty percent to break.

327
00:18:45,864 --> 00:18:51,384
It needs to reach a prior threshold, which we call the rational crime threshold:

328
00:18:51,823 --> 00:18:55,803
the point where productive people start concluding that building things

329
00:18:55,803 --> 00:18:58,124
is less rewarding than stealing them.

330
00:18:59,004 --> 00:19:03,563
The rational crime threshold is when stealing beats building for individuals.

331
00:19:04,404 --> 00:19:08,824
Terminal parasitic load is when enough individuals have crossed that threshold

332
00:19:08,824 --> 00:19:10,984
that the civilization cannot recover.

333
00:19:11,704 --> 00:19:12,824
The first is a temperature.

334
00:19:13,444 --> 00:19:15,484
The second is the fever that kills you.

335
00:19:16,304 --> 00:19:19,984
The historical evidence says the fever starts at thirty-five percent and

336
00:19:19,984 --> 00:19:21,404
kills at fifty percent.

337
00:19:22,244 --> 00:19:28,004
Your destructive economy (military plus cybercrime alone, not counting corruption,

338
00:19:28,104 --> 00:19:31,524
not counting the shadow economy, not counting the Political Dysfunction

339
00:19:31,524 --> 00:19:36,404
Tax) is at eleven point five percent and growing faster than your productive

340
00:19:36,404 --> 00:19:36,964
economy.

341
00:19:37,684 --> 00:19:41,624
At that rate, even the narrow metric crosses thirty-five percent by twenty

342
00:19:41,624 --> 00:19:42,384
thirty-seven.

343
00:19:42,924 --> 00:19:44,684
But that is the narrow metric.

344
00:19:45,104 --> 00:19:48,904
The real total, including all the things you are not counting, is higher.

345
00:19:49,404 --> 00:19:51,664
Every percent higher moves the timeline forward.

346
00:19:52,484 --> 00:19:53,184
Here is the loop.

347
00:19:53,684 --> 00:19:57,364
Your governments print money to fund military spending, which devalues wages

348
00:19:57,364 --> 00:20:00,384
through inflation, which makes legitimate work pay less,

349
00:20:01,024 --> 00:20:04,884
which pushes talent toward the destructive economy, which grows, which justifies

350
00:20:04,884 --> 00:20:06,664
more military spending.

351
00:20:07,304 --> 00:20:09,264
Meanwhile, every country the U.S.

352
00:20:09,264 --> 00:20:12,744
has bombed, sanctioned, or regime-changed has learned a lesson:

353
00:20:13,644 --> 00:20:17,924
conventional military resistance against Western economies is suicide, but

354
00:20:17,924 --> 00:20:22,144
draining them through cyber operations is cheap, effective, and essentially

355
00:20:22,144 --> 00:20:22,784
unpunished.

356
00:20:23,464 --> 00:20:28,224
You spent decades teaching adversarial nations that their only viable strategy

357
00:20:28,224 --> 00:20:31,524
is to parasitize your productive economy from the inside.

358
00:20:32,004 --> 00:20:33,964
They were excellent students.

359
00:20:34,064 --> 00:20:37,724
North Korea cannot build an aircraft carrier, but it can steal one point

360
00:20:37,724 --> 00:20:40,964
five billion dollars in cryptocurrency in a single afternoon.

361
00:20:41,924 --> 00:20:45,224
That is the rational response to the incentive structure you built.

362
00:20:45,944 --> 00:20:49,604
Domestically, the rational crime threshold is already here.

363
00:20:50,324 --> 00:20:54,604
Cybercrime has a higher return on investment than most legitimate businesses,

364
00:20:54,904 --> 00:20:57,164
and ninety-nine percent of it goes unpunished.

365
00:20:57,964 --> 00:21:02,524
When a software engineer can earn more in a week of ransomware than in a

366
00:21:02,524 --> 00:21:03,944
year of building products,

367
00:21:04,864 --> 00:21:08,844
crossing the rational crime threshold is not a moral failure.

368
00:21:08,964 --> 00:21:10,274
It is an economic one.

369
00:21:10,924 --> 00:21:15,044
You made legitimate work pay poorly by diverting productive investment into

370
00:21:15,044 --> 00:21:18,664
destruction, then act surprised when people choose the option that pays.

371
00:21:19,624 --> 00:21:25,144
Every year the gap between "crime pays" and "work pays" gets wider, more

372
00:21:25,144 --> 00:21:27,504
talent flows to the wrong side of the ledger.

373
00:21:28,424 --> 00:21:32,644
This is a recruitment pipeline for the destructive economy, funded by the

374
00:21:32,644 --> 00:21:37,794
destructive economy, producing the poverty that feeds the destructive economy.

375
00:21:38,124 --> 00:21:42,124
The Optimal Governance Trajectory breaks this loop at every link.

376
00:21:42,964 --> 00:21:46,904
Redirect military spending to medical research and you stop manufacturing

377
00:21:46,904 --> 00:21:47,844
the poverty.

378
00:21:48,544 --> 00:21:52,244
Cure diseases and you make the workforce productive enough that legitimate

379
00:21:52,244 --> 00:21:54,724
work pays better than crime.

380
00:21:54,724 --> 00:21:59,164
Make everyone richer and you eliminate the economic desperation that drives

381
00:21:59,164 --> 00:22:02,404
both state-sponsored hacking and individual cybercrime.

382
00:22:03,164 --> 00:22:06,614
You do not solve cybercrime with better firewalls.

383
00:22:06,944 --> 00:22:11,664
You solve it by making the productive economy so rewarding that crime becomes

384
00:22:11,664 --> 00:22:12,504
irrational.

385
00:22:13,244 --> 00:22:14,264
You do not outlaw theft.

386
00:22:14,824 --> 00:22:18,284
You make everyone rich enough that stealing becomes more effort than it

387
00:22:18,284 --> 00:22:18,784
is worth.

388
00:22:19,324 --> 00:22:20,744
The crime rate does not decline.

389
00:22:21,204 --> 00:22:22,704
It simply becomes pointless.

390
00:22:23,604 --> 00:22:25,204
On this path, G.D.P.

391
00:22:25,424 --> 00:22:26,744
does not decline gracefully.

392
00:22:27,464 --> 00:22:29,024
Supply chains collapse.

393
00:22:29,104 --> 00:22:31,304
Institutions lose legitimacy.

394
00:22:31,424 --> 00:22:33,354
Regional conflicts merge.

395
00:22:33,544 --> 00:22:37,664
The experts who wrote papers about "strategic equilibrium" would write new

396
00:22:37,664 --> 00:22:42,004
papers explaining why the old papers were still basically correct, but the

397
00:22:42,004 --> 00:22:43,264
